{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "922746ab-3bc0-87ec-961e-92d25add6eca",
  "created_at": "2026-03-12T11:41:45-04:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Conceicao Souza",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Priya Raman",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:38:54-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Utilities billing, this is Priya. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:38:58-04:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, hi. I just bought a house and the first water and sewer bill came in the previous owner's name. Not mine."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:39:07-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, I can look into that. What's the service address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:39:11-04:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four twenty-three Narragansett Avenue. Can you hear me okay? I've got one bar here."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:39:17-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can hear you fine. Four twenty-three Narragansett Avenue. Do you have the bill in front of you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:39:24-04:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I do. I've got the paper one right here. It says, um, it's dated February twenty-seventh. And the name on it is the guy I bought from. [line breaks up] I closed on the house in, well, after that."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:39:38-04:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sorry, you broke up for a second. Did you say the bill is dated February twenty-seventh?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:39:44-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. February twenty-seventh. Same thing I said. Why is it still his name? I have the deed."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:39:51-04:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's common, actually. The account stays in the seller's name until the city gets notice of the ownership change and a final reading is done. Then a new account is set up in your name. Bills in the meantime go out under the old one."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:40:07-04:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So who pays this one? I don't want to pay for his water. And I don't want my name getting mixed up in his balance."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:40:17-04:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I understand. I'd need to pull the account and see what period that bill covers and whether a final reading was recorded at the closing. If it covers time before you owned the home, it would generally be the prior owner's responsibility."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:40:32-04:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Generally. Great. Look, can you put that in writing? Because I know how this goes. I call, somebody says one thing, and then in two months I get a shutoff notice."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:40:44-04:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, I can send you a written explanation once I've reviewed the account. Is the mailing address four twenty-three Narragansett?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:40:52-04:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, that's it. [crosstalk] Or you can call me back, the number is four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-seven-six."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:40:58-04:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-seven-six. I'll note both the mail and the callback. Can I have the spelling of your last name?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:41:07-04:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "S-O-U-Z-A. Conceicao is the first name. C-O-N-C-E-I-C-A-O."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:41:10-04:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you, Ms. Souza. I'll review the account today and get the letter out. It should explain which charges are tied to the prior owner and how your new account will be set up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:41:23-04:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Fine. I've got enough on my plate. I'm supposed to be writing a speech for a retirement dinner and I've been standing here with this bill instead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:41:33-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'm sorry for the extra hassle. We'll get this sorted so you can get back to it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:41:40-04:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Thanks. Bye."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:41:42-04:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Goodbye, and have a good afternoon."
    }
  ],
